# Project architecture

- Stack: Node.js, TypeScript, Express, PostgreSQL, Knex.
- Layout: route → controller → service → model. Do not skip layers.
- Routes only wire paths to controllers. Controllers validate and call services. Services own business logic. Models own Knex CRUD only.
- Default API port: `3001`. CORS must allow `http://localhost:3000` and `CORS_ORIGIN`.
- Errors always return JSON: `{ "error": "Human-readable message" }` with `400` / `404` / `500`.
- PDF generation is out of scope for this API. Frontend owns PDF via Next.js.
- Resume files: `POST /services/s3/upload` → S3 + `s3_files` metadata, or Cloudinary upload. Frontend sends the URL as `resumeLink`. Before the LLM call, resolve the file and send resume + form answers to OpenRouter.
- Assessment scoring/content is produced by OpenRouter LLM JSON — do not reintroduce deterministic scoring logic in services. Services orchestrate (validate, call LLM, persist); the model returns the Assessment JSON.
- Email uses Nodemailer SMTP to the assessment contact email; do not keep an `email_sent` DB column or `status` on the report JSON.
- Report JSON fields only: `id`, `routeId`, `customerName`, `customerEmail`, `summary`, `headline`, `confidenceScore`, `breakdown`, `strengths`, `improvements`, `priorityImprovements`, `overallRecommendation`.
